Got it. Here’s a single WLST/Jython script that:
	•	Connects to DEV, reads all JDBC datasources and the DbAdapter plan (so it knows which connection-instances point to which datasource JNDIs).
	•	Connects to your LOCAL Admin, creates the same JDBC datasources (same names/JNDI/driver/url/properties) and targets them to DefaultServer (or first server if DefaultServer is missing).
	•	Ensures the DbAdapter on LOCAL has matching connection-instances and points each one to the same datasource JNDI as on DEV (via DataSourceName / xADataSourceName property overrides in the plan), then redeploys DbAdapter so changes take effect.

ASCII-only, WLST-safe (no with open, no ternaries, no emojis).

